# THE TIDE REAPER AS A SET PIECE (roadmap slice 1, step 4), over the shoulder
# with the tempered knife (steel bites its plate: tours/reaper_plating.tour).
# Its first sight is revealed -- it stands at its work, and the staged look
# (42_stage) hands back inside 3 s -- then its tell stands in its body, and it falls: the
# arch breaks and the hulk is left on the shore. The other way, the tide flats,
# is tours/reaper_tide.tour.
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/reaper_set_piece.tour --seed=7 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --held=knife_shear --config=unharmed
coast calm
tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
near keeper
wait 0.8
shot 01-its-first-sight-at-its-work with shoulder,mob:sentinel.coast,sentinel_revealing
await sentinel 12
wait 2.6

# Its tell stands in its body: the arch rears and the drum comes up into sight.
try 4
  walkto mob 6
  await tell 14
end
shot 02-the-arch-rears-its-tell with shoulder,mob:sentinel.coast

# Its fall. Taking it down by force is the pass above again and again: proved
# in the real simulation, through the openings it gives, by
# tests/sentinel/test_fight.gd, and a scripted player fed to it pass after pass
# is luck. What these frames are of is the fall itself: the arch breaks, and the
# hulk it leaves on the shore.
fell sentinel.coast
await sentinel_dead 3
wait 0.6
shot 03-the-arch-breaks with shoulder,sentinel_dead
wait 2.4
shot 04-it-lies-across-the-shore with shoulder,sentinel_dead
